{
  "summary": "Η Αμαλία διαβάζει ένα παλιό δείγμα ανακοίνωσης που περιγράφει σβήσιμο προηγούμενων σημειώσεων και ακύρωση συναντήσεων, αλλά εξηγεί ότι αυτό δεν αντιστοιχεί στην πραγματική κατάσταση. Στην πραγματικότητα, δύο συναντήσεις επιβεβαιώθηκαν (μία στην αίθουσα Β), μία τρίτη περιμένει απάντηση. Ο Θωμάς ρωτά αν η εκκρεμής συνάντηση θα μεταφερθεί στο διαδίκτυο, αλλά η Αμαλία απαντά ότι δεν έχει αποφασιστεί. Η τελική απόφαση είναι να δημοσιευτεί μόνο το πρόγραμμα των δύο επιβεβαιωμένων συναντήσεων με τη σωστή αίθουσα Β, ενώ η τρίτη θα προστεθεί μετά την απάντηση του εισηγητή. Καμία από τις δύο επιβεβαιωμένες συναντήσεις δεν ακυρώθηκε.",
  "key_points": [
    "Δύο συναντήσεις επιβεβαιώθηκαν (μία στην αίθουσα Β)",
    "Μία τρίτη συνάντηση περιμένει απάντηση από τον εισηγητή",
    "Η εκκρεμής συνάντηση δεν έχει αποφασιστεί για μεταφορά στο διαδίκτυο",
    "Καμία από τις δύο επιβεβαιωμένες συναντήσεις δεν ακυρώθηκε"
  ],
  "chapter_title": "Προγραμματισμός συναντήσεων: επιβεβαιωμένες και εκκρεμείς"
}

{
  "notes": "Nadia proposed East Hall on 14 September for 36 visitors; details provisional due to unconfirmed building manager. Harun checks venue/access, Erin manages budget/receipts, Celeste reviews volunteer instructions; borrowed games return with pieces/instructions. Team set €180 spending limit; preliminary estimate €146.20 unaccepted, no payments. Refreshments recorded separately. Three activity types: quiet, cooperative, supervised tables; visitors move between tables if seats free, no requirement to finish games. Neighbours lend games; volunteers count pieces twice, photograph for checks but not proof of loss. Starting inventory records missing pieces. Harun ensures clear route, inspects room before publishing access details; no claim on mobility aids fitting. Volunteer rota draft: 6 confirmed, 4 expressions of interest; Celeste contacts for clear answers. Public announcement won't claim 10 trained volunteers until confirmations/briefing complete. Briefing explains welcoming newcomers: volunteers read/demonstrate turns, ask before handling cards/pieces; aim is help without dictating play style.",
  "chapter_title": "Community Board-Game Day Planning"
}

{
  "notes": "A draft registration form requested preferred arrival period and optional contact address, not age, employer, or personal story. Nadia wanted short sign-up process for informal event. Erin clarified contact address does not grant permission for public mailing or promotional messages. Group agreed photos of game layouts useful but recognizable visitors require separate permission; participation does not imply photo consent. No general permission to publish full recording agreed. Quentin showed misleading sample notice claiming all seats booked; team discussed why attractive layout doesn't make statement true; no real booking list existed. Celeste instructed volunteers to describe sample as training material without repeating its claim. Event has no entry fee but visitors may bring refreshments; no door donation decided; future fundraising needs separate announcement and accounting. East Hall potentially unavailable due to floor panel check; inspection doesn't close building; fallback plan to use West Hall prepared but no authority to confirm it yet; Nadia kept draft notice unpublished while Harun sought building manager's confirmation. Storage cupboard has folding signs and two display stands from neighbourhood association; items can be borrowed for day if returned clean and undamaged; not prizes; Celeste suggested labeling each item with owner before packing. Suggested timetable places volunteer briefing before visitors arrive and allows time for counting components; opening hour not fixed; Nadia rejected draft timetable as final public schedule; will check travel arrangements with confirmed volunteers before publishing opening/closing times.",
  "chapter_title": "Event Planning Decisions and Permissions"
}

{
  "notes": "Visitors could leave unsigned comments on explanation helpfulness. Complaints kept as wording without rewriting. Organisers discussed improvements but no survey results existed. East Hall unavailable on proposed date; West Hall available 21 September with 28 visitors (vs 36). Nadia and Erin accepted West Hall arrangement. Venue and date confirmed; volunteer shifts not confirmed. Final public plan: West Hall 21 September, 28 visitors, no entry fee, €180 spending limit. Nadia to update unpublished notice before sharing. Harun to complete access check in West Hall. Erin to authorise purchase after final equipment quote. Actions remain future tasks. No purchases, briefing, or access inspection completed. Nadia to publish schedule after practical checks; photo permissions separate from participation. Old venue proposal and fictional fully-booked notice not current. Event planned but not yet held.",
